  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-galerkin-coarse-grid-correction": [
      "## Definition\n\nWork over the real field with standard coordinate inner products. Let\n$A_h\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$ be symmetric positive definite (equivalently,\npositive definite in the Cholesky convention of\n[[def-cholesky-factorisation-with-positive-diagonal]]) and let\n$P\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times m}$ have full column rank, where $1\\le m\\le n$.\nThe map $P$ sends coarse-grid coordinate vectors to fine-grid coordinate\nvectors; its Euclidean adjoint is the transpose $P^{\\mathsf T}$ by\n[[thm-matrix-of-the-adjoint-is-the-conjugate-transpose]]. Define the **Galerkin\ncoarse matrix**\n\n$$A_H:=P^{\\mathsf T}A_hP.$$\n\nWhenever $A_H$ is invertible, define the **exact Galerkin coarse-correction\nerror map**\n\n$$C:=I_n-PA_H^{-1}P^{\\mathsf T}A_h.$$\n\nThis definition is conditional on invertibility of $A_H$. The next theorem\nproves that condition from positive definiteness of $A_h$ and full column rank\nof $P$. The formula is in exact real arithmetic; a rediscretized operator is\nnot identified with $A_H$ unless equality is separately shown."
    ],
    "lem-zero-boundary-piecewise-affine-functions-lie-in-h1zero": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice. Let $v:[0,1]\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuous and affine\non each interval of a finite partition $0=x_0<x_1<\\cdots<x_N=1$, with\n$v(0)=v(1)=0$. Then the Sobolev class of $v$ belongs to\n$H^1_0(0,1)=W^{1,2}_0((0,1);\\mathbb R)$, where $W^{1,2}_0$ is the norm\nclosure of $C_c^\\infty(0,1)$ in $W^{1,2}(0,1)$."
    ],
    "thm-galerkin-coarse-correction-is-energy-orthogonal-projector": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $A_h\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$ be symmetric positive definite and let\n$P\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times m}$ have full column rank. Put\n$A_H=P^{\\mathsf T}A_hP$. Then $A_H$ is symmetric positive definite, hence\ninvertible, and the map $C=I_n-PA_H^{-1}P^{\\mathsf T}A_h$ of\n[[def-galerkin-coarse-grid-correction]] satisfies\n\n$$C^2=C,\\qquad CP=0,\\qquad P^{\\mathsf T}A_hC=0,\\qquad C^{\\mathsf T}A_h=A_hC.$$\n\nConsequently $\\operatorname{Ran}(C)=\\operatorname{Ran}(P)^{\\perp_{A_h}}$;\n$C$ is the orthogonal projector onto that complement in the energy inner\nproduct $\\langle x,y\\rangle_{A_h}:=x^{\\mathsf T}A_hy$."
    ],
    "def-symmetric-two-grid-error-operator": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $A_h$ be symmetric positive definite, let $C$ be the Galerkin projector\nof [[thm-galerkin-coarse-correction-is-energy-orthogonal-projector]], and let\n$S\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$ be a linear pre-smoothing error map. For the\nenergy inner product of [[def-energy-inner-product-and-norm-for-a-hermitian-positive-definite-matrix]],\ndefine the **$A_h$-adjoint** of $S$ by\n\n$$S^{*_{A_h}}:=A_h^{-1}S^{\\mathsf T}A_h.$$\n\nThis is well-defined because $A_h$ is invertible. For all $x,y$,\n$\\langle Sx,y\\rangle_{A_h}=x^{\\mathsf T}S^{\\mathsf T}A_hy\n=\\langle x,S^{*_{A_h}}y\\rangle_{A_h}$, so it is the adjoint with respect to\nthat energy inner product. The **symmetric two-grid error map** is\n\n$$E:=S^{*_{A_h}}CS.$$\n\nIt maps an input error through pre-smoothing $S$, exact coarse correction $C$,\nand the $A_h$-adjoint post-smoother."
    ],
    "alg-aggregation-based-algebraic-multigrid-hierarchy": [
      "## Definition\n\nThis is a finite aggregation-based algebraic multigrid **setup** procedure; it\nconstructs a hierarchy and does not claim that any cycle converges. All\narithmetic and comparisons below are exact. An admissible input consists of an\ninteger $n_0\\ge1$, a real symmetric positive-definite matrix\n$A_0=(a_{ij})\\in\\mathbb R^{n_0\\times n_0}$ whose off-diagonal\nentries satisfy $a_{ij}\\le0$, a real threshold $0<\\theta<1$, a coarse-size\nthreshold $n_{\\min}\\ge1$, and a level cap $L\\ge0$. A matrix with these sign\nand definiteness conditions is the matrix class used here. The terms\n**strength graph**, **aggregate**, **prolongation**, and **Galerkin hierarchy**\nare defined by the steps below.\n\n1. Set $\\ell=0$, $n_\\ell=\\dim A_\\ell$, and retain $A_\\ell$ in the output. If\n   $n_\\ell\\le n_{\\min}$, return status `coarse-reached`.\n2. If $\\ell=L$ before the stop test in step 1 succeeds, return status\n   `level-cap`.\n3. On vertices $1,\\ldots,n_\\ell$, place an undirected edge $\\{i,j\\}$ for\n   $i\\ne j$ exactly when $a_{ij}^{(\\ell)}<0$ and at least one of\n   $$-a_{ij}^{(\\ell)}\\ge\\theta\\max_{k\\ne i}(-a_{ik}^{(\\ell)}),\\qquad -a_{ij}^{(\\ell)}\\ge\\theta\\max_{k\\ne j}(-a_{jk}^{(\\ell)})$$\n   holds. This finite graph is the strength graph at level $\\ell$.\n4. Let $U=\\{1,\\ldots,n_\\ell\\}$ and start with no aggregates. While $U\\ne\\varnothing$, let $i$ be the smallest element of $U$, create one aggregate\n   $$C_r=\\{i\\}\\cup\\bigl(N(i)\\cap U\\bigr),$$\n   where $N(i)$ is its strength-graph neighbour set, then remove every element of $C_r$ from $U$. This produces an ordered family of aggregates.\n5. Let $n_{\\ell+1}$ be the number of aggregates. If $n_{\\ell+1}\\ge n_\\ell$, return status `coarsening-stalled` with the hierarchy through level $\\ell$. Otherwise form the indicator prolongation\n   $$(P_\\ell)_{ir}=1\\text{ if }i\\in C_r,\\qquad (P_\\ell)_{ir}=0\\text{ otherwise},$$\n   form the Galerkin coarse matrix $A_{\\ell+1}=P_\\ell^{\\mathsf T}A_\\ell P_\\ell$, append $P_\\ell,A_{\\ell+1}$, replace $\\ell$ by $\\ell+1$, and return to step 1.\n\nThe result contains all completed matrices and prolongations and exactly one\nstatus: `coarse-reached`, `level-cap`, or `coarsening-stalled`. Reaching any\nstatus is not a convergence or quality certificate."
    ],
    "lem-one-dimensional-poisson-smoothing-and-approximation": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $N=2M\\ge4$, $h=1/N$, and let $A_h\\in\\mathbb R^{(N-1)\\times(N-1)}$ have diagonal $2/h$, adjacent off-diagonal entries $-1/h$, and all other entries zero. This is the Dirichlet stiffness matrix for the uniform one-dimensional Poisson mesh. Let $P\\in\\mathbb R^{(N-1)\\times(M-1)}$ linearly interpolate from the coarse nodes at even fine indices: set coarse endpoint values $v_0=v_M=0$, $(Pv)_{2j}=v_j$, and $(Pv)_{2j+1}=(v_j+v_{j+1})/2$ wherever these are interior fine indices. Put $A_H=P^{\\mathsf T}A_hP$, $C=I-PA_H^{-1}P^{\\mathsf T}A_h$, and $S=I-A_h/\\lambda_{\\max}(A_h)$. Then for every integer $\\nu\\ge1$ and every fine vector $e$,\n\n$$\\|CS^\\nu e\\|_{A_h}^2\\le\\frac{2}{2\\nu+1}\\|e\\|_{A_h}^2.$$\n\nThe separate estimates proved below are the exact approximation bound\n$\\|Cw\\|_{A_h}^2\\le(h/2)\\|A_hw\\|_2^2$ and smoothing bound\n$\\|A_hS^\\nu e\\|_2^2\\le4\\,[h(2\\nu+1)]^{-1}\\|e\\|_{A_h}^2$; their constants are compatible and independent of $N$."
    ],
    "alg-finite-galerkin-v-cycle": [
      "## Definition\n\nFix a finite Galerkin hierarchy of real SPD matrices\n$A_j\\in\\mathbb R^{n_j\\times n_j}$, $0\\le j\\le J$, with $n_j\\ge1$, and\nfull-column-rank prolongations $P_j\\in\\mathbb R^{n_j\\times n_{j-1}}$\nsatisfying $A_{j-1}=P_j^{\\mathsf T}A_jP_j$ for $1\\le j\\le J$. Choose\nnonnegative integer sweep counts $\\nu_1,\\nu_2$, a positive integer cycle\ncount $\\gamma$, and matrices $K_j^{\\mathrm{pre}},K_j^{\\mathrm{post}}\\in\n\\mathbb R^{n_j\\times n_j}$ for $1\\le j\\le J$; $^{\\mathsf T}$ denotes the\ntranspose of [[def-transpose-of-a-matrix]]. An invocation\n$\\operatorname{Cycle}(j,x,b)$ takes $x,b\\in\\mathbb R^{n_j}$ and returns an\napproximate solution to $A_jz=b$:\n\n1. If $j=0$, return the exact solution $A_0^{-1}b$.\n2. Starting from $x$, perform $\\nu_1$ pre-sweeps\n   $x\\leftarrow x+K_j^{\\mathrm{pre}}(b-A_jx)$ and set $r=b-A_jx$.\n3. Set $e=0$. For $t=1,\\ldots,\\gamma$, replace $e$ by the recursive iterate\n   $$e\\leftarrow\\operatorname{Cycle}(j-1,e,P_j^{\\mathsf T}r).$$\n4. Correct $x\\leftarrow x+P_je$, then perform $\\nu_2$ post-sweeps\n   $x\\leftarrow x+K_j^{\\mathrm{post}}(b-A_jx)$; return $x$.\n\nThe V-cycle is $\\gamma=1$ and the W-cycle is $\\gamma=2$. Each call decreases\n$j$, so the recursion is finite. The definition fixes exact arithmetic; setup\ncost, floating-point error, and convergence of the recursive cycle are separate\nclaims."
    ],
    "thm-two-grid-energy-contraction-under-joint-estimate": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $A_h$, $C$, $S$, and $E=S^{*_{A_h}}CS$ be as in\n[[def-symmetric-two-grid-error-operator]]. Suppose $0\\le\\rho<1$ and\n\n$$\\|CSx\\|_{A_h}^2\\le\\rho\\|x\\|_{A_h}^2\\qquad\\text{for every }x\\in\\mathbb R^n.$$\n\nThen $E$ is self-adjoint and nonnegative in the $A_h$ inner product, and its\noperator norm induced by $\\|\\cdot\\|_{A_h}$ satisfies $\\|E\\|_{A_h}\\le\\rho$.\nA rate derived from separate smoothing and approximation inequalities requires\na proof that those inequalities imply this joint estimate."
    ],
    "thm-aggregation-amg-hierarchy-preserves-spd-and-terminates": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor every admissible input to\n[[alg-aggregation-based-algebraic-multigrid-hierarchy]], each successful\naggregation partitions the current indices into nonempty disjoint sets. Its\nindicator prolongation has full column rank. Every successful Galerkin product\n$A_{\\ell+1}=P_\\ell^{\\mathsf T}A_\\ell P_\\ell$ is symmetric positive definite\nwith nonpositive off-diagonal entries. The setup procedure terminates after at\nmost $L$ coarsening attempts and returns exactly one of `coarse-reached`,\n`level-cap`, or `coarsening-stalled`. These structural properties do not imply\nmultigrid convergence."
    ],
    "thm-galerkin-v-cycle-work-recurrence-master-regimes": [
      "## Statement\n\nSuppose each level with $N$ unknowns has $cN$ arithmetic work outside\nrecursion, its next level has $N/q$ unknowns for a fixed $q=2^d>1$, the base\nsolve at $N=1$ has bounded positive cost, and each cycle makes $\\gamma\\ge1$\nrecursive calls as in [[alg-finite-galerkin-v-cycle]]. For $N=q^L$ the work\nrecurrence\n\n$$T(N)=cN+\\gamma T(N/q)$$\n\nhas order $\\Theta(N)$ when $\\gamma<q$, $\\Theta(N\\log N)$ when $\\gamma=q$,\nand $\\Theta(N^{\\log_q\\gamma})$ when $\\gamma>q$. These are arithmetic-work\nbounds conditional on the stated uniform per-level cost and coarsening\nassumptions. They do not imply convergence or include setup cost."
    ],
    "thm-one-dimensional-poisson-two-grid-energy-contraction": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor the nested one-dimensional Poisson grids and prolongation of\n[[lem-one-dimensional-poisson-smoothing-and-approximation]], take the\npre-smoothing error map to be $S^\\nu$, with $S=I-A_h/\\lambda_{\\max}(A_h)$,\nand take the post-smoother to be its $A_h$-adjoint. The resulting symmetric\ntwo-grid error map satisfies\n\n$$\\|E\\|_{A_h}\\le\\frac{2}{2\\nu+1}\\le\\frac23<1\\qquad(\\nu\\ge1),$$\n\nuniformly for all even $N=2M\\ge4$. This proves one concrete level-uniform\ntwo-grid rate; it does not assert convergence of an arbitrary AMG hierarchy."
    ],
